    <string name="usage_access">Usage access</string>
    <string name="usage_access_sub">Notices when you open an app you chose to block</string>
    <string name="usage_access_disclosure">To lock the apps you pick, the app needs to know which app is open right now. It only compares that with your own blocked and allowed lists, and never stores or shares it.\n\nThe app has no internet access, so this can\'t leave your phone.\n\nOn the next screen, turn Usage access on for this app. You\'ll be brought back here automatically.</string>
    <string name="overlay">Display over other apps</string>
    <string name="overlay_sub">Shows your checklist over blocked apps, and your buddy</string>
    <string name="overlay_disclosure">"This lets the app:\n\n  - show your checklist on top of an app you chose to block,\n  - bring the checklist back when Focus lock is on (only if you turn it on),\n  - show your buddy walking on screen (you can turn it off any time).\n\nIt never draws over apps you didn\'t pick, and never imitates system screens."</string>
